{%- comment -%}
  [[hours_sw]] / [[hours_ne]] inside an answer render that shop's week from
  pt-nap (store_hours metaobject), so FAQ hours can't drift from the footer.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- capture pt_hours_sw %}{% render 'pt-nap', location: 'sw', field: 'hours_line' %}{% endcapture -%}
{%- capture pt_hours_ne %}{% render 'pt-nap', location: 'ne', field: 'hours_line' %}{% endcapture -%}
{%- assign pt_hours_sw = pt_hours_sw | strip_newlines | strip -%}
{%- assign pt_hours_ne = pt_hours_ne | strip_newlines | strip -%}
<div class="faq-home">
  <div class="faq-home__container">

    <div class="faq-home__top">
      <div class="faq-home__header">
        <span class="faq-home__eyebrow">{{ section.settings.eyebrow }}</span>
        <h2 class="faq-home__heading">{{ section.settings.heading }}</h2>
      </div>

      {%- comment -%}
        The CTA used to fall back to href="#" when no link was set, which shipped
        a dead "Contact us" button on the live homepage. Now it falls back to the
        contact page, and renders only when there's both a label and a target.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- assign faq_cta_link = section.settings.cta_link | default: '/pages/contact' -%}
      {%- if section.settings.cta_label != blank and faq_cta_link != blank -%}
        <a href="{{ faq_cta_link }}" class="faq-home__cta">
          {{ section.settings.cta_label }}
          <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M5 12h14M12 5l7 7-7 7"/></svg>
        </a>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    <div class="faq-home__grid">
      {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
        {%- if block.settings.question != blank and block.settings.answer != blank -%}
          <details class="faq-home__card" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
            <summary class="faq-home__question">
              <span class="faq-home__q-text">{{ block.settings.question }}</span>
              <span class="faq-home__q-icon">
                <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                  <path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/>
                </svg>
              </span>
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-home__answer">
              {{ block.settings.answer | replace: '[[hours_sw]]', pt_hours_sw | replace: '[[hours_ne]]', pt_hours_ne }}
            </div>
          </details>
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>

  </div>
</div>

{%- comment -%}
  FAQPage schema. Only complete Q+A pairs are emitted — a half-filled block used
  to publish an empty acceptedAnswer, which Google treats as invalid markup.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign faq_valid = 0 -%}
{%- for block in section.blocks -%}
  {%- if block.settings.question != blank and block.settings.answer != blank -%}
    {%- assign faq_valid = faq_valid | plus: 1 -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- if faq_valid > 0 -%}
  <script type="application/ld+json">
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "FAQPage",
    "mainEntity": [
      {%- assign faq_i = 0 -%}
      {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
        {%- if block.settings.question != blank and block.settings.answer != blank -%}
          {%- if faq_i > 0 -%},{%- endif -%}
          {%- assign faq_i = faq_i | plus: 1 -%}
          {
            "@type": "Question",
            "name": {{ block.settings.question | json }},
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "@type": "Answer",
              "text": {{ block.settings.answer | replace: '[[hours_sw]]', pt_hours_sw | replace: '[[hours_ne]]', pt_hours_ne | strip_html | json }}
            }
          }
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
    ]
  }
  </script>
{%- endif -%}

{% stylesheet %}
  .faq-home {
    background: #fff;
    padding: 7rem 0;
  }

  .faq-home__container {
    max-width: 1400px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 6rem;
  }

  .faq-home__top {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-end;
    justify-content: space-between;
    margin-bottom: 4rem;
  }

  .faq-home__header {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }

  .faq-home__eyebrow {
    font-family: 'Outfit', sans-serif;
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    font-weight: 400;
    color: #dc2626;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  }

  .faq-home__heading {
    font-family: 'Barlow Condensed', sans-serif;
    font-size: 3rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: #111;
    margin: 0;
    line-height: 1.1;
  }

  .faq-home__cta {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    font-family: 'Outfit', sans-serif;
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: #dc2626;
    text-decoration: none;
    white-space: nowrap;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    transition: gap 0.2s;
  }

  .faq-home__cta:hover {
    gap: 0.8rem;
  }

  /* ── Wrapper ── */
  .faq-home__grid {
    background: #f7f7f7;
    border-radius: 8px;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  /* ── Card ── */
  .faq-home__card {
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.06);
  }

  .faq-home__card:last-child {
    border-bottom: none;
  }

  .faq-home__question {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1.6rem;
    padding: 1.4rem 2.4rem;
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style: none;
    font-family: 'Outfit', sans-serif;
    font-size: 1.4rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: #222;
    transition: color 0.2s, background 0.15s;
  }

  .faq-home__question::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }

  .faq-home__question:hover {
    color: #dc2626;
    background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.02);
  }

  .faq-home__q-text {
    flex: 1;
    line-height: 1.4;
  }

  .faq-home__q-icon {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    color: #9ca3af;
    transition: transform 0.3s ease, color 0.2s;
  }

  .faq-home__card[open] .faq-home__q-icon {
    transform: rotate(180deg);
    color: #dc2626;
  }

  .faq-home__card[open] .faq-home__question {
    color: #dc2626;
  }

  .faq-home__answer {
    font-family: 'Outfit', sans-serif;
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    font-weight: 300;
    color: #6b7280;
    line-height: 1.65;
    padding: 0 2.4rem 1.6rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .faq-home__container {
      padding: 0 2rem;
    }
    .faq-home__top {
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: flex-start;
      gap: 1.2rem;
    }
    .faq-home__heading {
      font-size: 2.4rem;
    }
    .faq-home__question {
      padding: 1.2rem 1.6rem;
    }
    .faq-home__answer {
      padding: 0 1.6rem 1.4rem;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 480px) {
    .faq-home {
      padding: 4rem 0;
    }
    .faq-home__container {
      padding: 0 1.6rem;
    }
    .faq-home__heading {
      font-size: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 2.4rem);
    }
    .faq-home__question {
      padding: 1.4rem 1.2rem;
      font-size: 1.4rem;
      min-height: 4.8rem;
      gap: 1.2rem;
    }
    .faq-home__answer {
      padding: 0 1.2rem 1.4rem;
      font-size: 1.2rem;
    }
    .faq-home__cta {
      font-size: 1.2rem;
      min-height: 4.4rem;
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
    }
    .faq-home__top {
      margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 360px) {
    .faq-home__container {
      padding: 0 1.2rem;
    }
    .faq-home__question {
      padding: 1.2rem 1rem;
      font-size: 1.3rem;
      gap: 1rem;
    }
    .faq-home__answer {
      padding: 0 1rem 1.2rem;
      font-size: 1.2rem;
      line-height: 1.5;
    }
    .faq-home__heading {
      font-size: 2rem;
    }
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "FAQ",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "section",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "eyebrow",
      "label": "Eyebrow",
      "default": "FAQ"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "heading",
      "label": "Heading",
      "default": "Frequently asked questions"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "cta_label",
      "label": "CTA label",
      "default": "Contact us"
    },
    {
      "type": "url",
      "id": "cta_link",
      "label": "CTA link",
      "info": "Defaults to /pages/contact if left empty."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Writing answers"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "These answers are published as FAQ structured data, so AI assistants and Google quote them directly. Keep every figure identical to the service pages. Never mention wheel alignment, mobile service, or winter tire storage — Prince Tires does not offer them."
    }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "question",
      "name": "Question",
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "question",
          "label": "Question"
        },
        {
          "type": "richtext",
          "id": "answer",
          "label": "Answer"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "FAQ",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What tire brands does Prince Tires carry?",
            "answer": "<p>We stock premium brands including Michelin, Bridgestone, Firestone, Continental, BFGoodrich, General, Toyo, Yokohama, Kumho and Cooper, plus value brands we import directly — Haida, Mileking, Rovelo and Cargomax trailer tires. That range means we can quote you a set at almost any budget. Call either shop with your tire size and we'll tell you exactly what's on the shelf.</p>"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Where is Prince Tires located in Calgary?",
            "answer": "<p>We have two Calgary shops. Our main location is 111 42 Ave SW, Calgary, AB T2G 0A4 — call (403) 452-4283. Our second shop is Unit 101, 3928 Edmonton Trail NE, Calgary, AB T2E 3P6 — call (825) 395-4024. The 42 Ave SW location carries the larger inventory, so if you need a specific size today, start there. Email us at info@princetires.ca.</p>"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What tire services does Prince Tires offer?",
            "answer": "<p>New tire sales, tire installation, computer balancing, tire rotation, flat and puncture repair, TPMS sensor service, and seasonal changeovers. Every install includes mounting, balancing, a valve stem check and torque to manufacturer spec — and we'll re-torque for free after you've driven on them. We're tire specialists, so we don't do wheel alignment.</p>"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How long does a tire installation take?",
            "answer": "<p>A standard set of four takes about 45 to 60 minutes, including computer balancing. Add TPMS work and it's closer to 90 minutes. Booking online lets us set a bay aside once we confirm your time and have your tires pulled before you arrive — walk-ins are welcome, but we can't promise same-visit availability during the October and November changeover rush.</p>"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How much does tire installation cost?",
            "answer": "<p>Installation is $30 a tire ($120 for four) on a car or SUV, whether you buy the tires from us or bring your own. It includes mounting, computer balancing, a valve stem check and torque to spec. TPMS sensor replacement is $60 per sensor. Leaving your old tires with us is included when you buy tires from us, and disposal is $5 per tire when you bring your own. When you bring your own tires, SUVs are $30 a tire and trucks $35 a tire. GST applies.</p>"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Do you sell winter tires for Calgary roads?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes, and they're our busiest category. Calgary's ice and freeze-thaw cycles are hard on tires, and we carry dedicated winter tires as well as 3PMSF-rated all-weather options if you'd rather run one set year-round. Winter tires start around $130 per tire installed. Book early — the changeover rush runs mid-October to mid-November and slots go fast.</p>"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
